WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
 Fast mode is available on opus 4.8, same model, roughly 2.5 the speed and 3 times cheaper

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.040
 than before.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:14.080
 Fast mode is 2.5 the speed, but 3 times more expensive than normal mode.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.080
 What does it do?

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.040
 It actually gives you priority in the line when you're waiting for an answer?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.360
 It's the time of computing before you get the answer, it just goes way faster.

